note """
The CROSS-MODULE emission path, pinned by the golden set rather than only by the
end-to-end run. Three things about the emitted file are the point, and each is
invisible in a run that merely succeeds: the upstream flow's funcs are SPLICED in
(Screenable is declared here though nothing in this file wrote it), the flow-only
import is DROPPED (no Go name here is qualified with it, so emitting it would
produce an unused import), and the imported flow gets NO wiring function of its
own -- only WireCrossmodule appears.
"""
import "example.com/upstream"

flow crossmodule
source ingest Poll()
use s upstream.Screen from ingest -> ok, bad
sink store Store from ok
drop bad
